# Fixtures under tests/data/ are committed on purpose: the C++ suite must run without a Python
# toolchain, and the conformance fixture is the record of what XRADIO actually writes. Only the
# intermediate FITS the conformance generator writes is transient, and it deletes that itself.

# Instructions for coding agents are each contributor's own, not part of the repository.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Working documents stay local: research drafts, in a language other than the project's and no longer
# kept in step with the code. What a reader of this repository needs is in the README, CONTEXT.md,
# docs/storage-tuning.md and the ADRs.
docs/archive/
docs/read-api.md
docs/sidecar.md
